e-raise.  \n\nA raise of 400 is reasonable to apply pressure and possibly take the pot now, or build a bigger pot for when I hit. But my opponent has shown strength, so they may not fold. Still, with strong draws, semi-bluff raising is good.  \n\nGiven my chip stack (19400) and this being early in the match, I want to play aggressively but not overly risky. Raising to 400 is a good balance—it builds the pot, gives me fold equity, and keeps me in control. Checking (just calling) is passive and gives a free turn card; raising is better. All-in is excessive.  \n\nReason: I have a flush draw plus gutshot straight draw, giving me strong equity (~48%) against likely top pair. A semi-bluff raise of 400 applies pressure, builds the pot for when I hit, and may cause opponent to fold marginal hands. It’s a standard play in this situation.  \n\nAnswer: 400"}
