it and bet, or could face a raise now.  \n\nOverall, checking seems the most balanced—preserve chips, see river, decide then.  \n\nReason: I have a decent draw with 8 outs, but no made hand yet. My opponent has shown passive play by calling. By checking, I avoid bloating the pot out of position with a marginal drawing hand, and I can reevaluate on the river. If I bet small, I risk a raise and might have to fold, wasting my equity. Checking keeps the pot controlled.  \n\nAnswer: 0'}
